WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.460
- I don't know if you've
read, Carl Jung said

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:08.150
that the greatest danger
that humanity faces

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:12.670
is not from any external
force like natural disasters

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:17.270
or diseases or pandemics.

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:20.350
He said the greatest
danger that humanity faces

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:24.233
is a collective psychosis.

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:29.990
So to some extent, I see it
happening, not quite as extreme

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:34.820
yet as in places like
Maoist China or Cambodia

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:39.820
where 1/3 of the population
got murdered in Cambodia.

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:47.560
Absurd, totally absurd ideas
taking over people's minds.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:52.483
For example, in Cambodia, we
were there a few years ago,

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:59.000
at the time of Pol Pot,
the Cambodian mad dictator,

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:05.930
anybody who could read
and write or anybody,

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:08.770
if you wear glasses, you
were an enemy of the people

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:11.210
because you were regarded as the oppressor

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:14.130
and likely to be killed.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:15.580
You had to show your hands.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:18.305
You're not doing manual work,

00:01:18.305 --> 00:01:22.392
you're one of the enemies of the people.

00:01:22.392 --> 00:01:25.892
(warm instrumental music)

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:30.820
- I'm Dave Rubin and joining me today

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:32.950
is one of the most widely recognized

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:35.460
spiritual teachers on the planet.

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:37.270
His book, "The Power of Now"

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:40.630
sold 12 million, that's million copies,

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:45.010
and the followup, "A New Earth"
sold over 15 million copies.

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:48.510
Both have been translated
in over 50 languages.

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:51.840
My friend Eckhart Tolle, welcome
back to "The Rubin Report."

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.532
- Thank you, Dave, nice to see you again.

00:01:54.532 --> 00:01:56.349
- It's great to talk to you.

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:57.940
As my audience knows,

00:01:57.940 --> 00:01:59.680
we are at the beginning
of August right now,

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:02.180
and I am technically off the grid.

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:05.510
I am in an undisclosed
location with no technology,

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:10.020
no phone, no computer,
no news, no nothing.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:11.810
So we're taping this at the end of July,

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:13.220
and I thought you would
be the right person

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:15.575
to sort of kick this month off with.

00:02:15.575 --> 00:02:18.329
So before we get to sort
of the off the grid stuff

00:02:18.329 --> 00:02:22.420
and digital detox, I wanted
to ask you just sort of,

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:27.420
what do you make of the
spiritual health of the planet

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:29.360
in this last year and a half,

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:31.620
this sort of crazy year and a half

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:33.220
that we've all had to deal with?

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:39.630
- Yes, I believe crazy
is quite a good word

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:43.620
to describe it in many ways.

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:46.710
There's been many collective challenges.

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:51.710
The main one is the
virus and the lockdowns

00:02:52.607 --> 00:02:55.703
and various other challenges.

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:02.070
I've had this strange feeling,
idea in the past few months

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:06.720
that a certain segment of humanity

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:11.720
is losing the ability to think rationally.

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:19.850
There is a decrease in, I call
it IQ or whatever it may be.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:26.510
There's a diminishment of
rational faculty as reflected

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:31.780
in many ways on mainstream
media, social media and so on.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.450
And another segment of humanity

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:41.450
is actually becoming more aware,
more aware, more conscious,

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:46.580
is not drawn into the regressive phase

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:50.970
that some of humanity
may be going through.

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:55.730
It's not unusual for humanity
to occasionally collectively

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:58.290
regress to a lower state of consciousness.

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:03.290
It just happened whenever
a country or collective

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:08.910
has been taken over by an almost,

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:11.940
one could say toxic ideology

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:14.720
that has completely taken possession

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:17.303
of millions of people's minds.

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:22.159
Look at of course, National
Socialism in Germany.

00:04:22.159 --> 00:04:26.120
The Maoist Cultural
Revolution was quite crazy.

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:28.883
What happened in Cambodia under Pol Pot.

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:35.490
Totally crazy ideas invaded
millions of people's minds

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:40.090
and reduced their ability

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:43.440
to actually engage in rational thinking.

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:48.050
And things that happened,
for example, in Maoist China

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.763
during the Cultural Revolution,

00:04:51.691 --> 00:04:54.410
children reporting on their parents,

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:56.070
when they were angry with their parents.

00:04:56.070 --> 00:04:58.433
All they had to do is go to
school and report their parents,

00:04:58.433 --> 00:05:01.760
that they had said something
against the government.

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:04.870
The parents would be taken
away and never seen again.

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:07.620
They went around public parks

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:11.483
in big cities in China tearing out flowers

00:05:11.483 --> 00:05:15.210
because beauty was
regarded as bourgeoisie.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:19.663
You had to kill your
pets, your dogs and cats.

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:25.603
And these are just a few
examples of totally toxic

00:05:25.603 --> 00:05:30.603
and irrational thoughts
taking over people's minds.

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:33.000
So that's, to some extent,

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:37.020
I've been seeing this
happening collectively,

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:40.000
not just in one country,
in quite a few Western,

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:43.103
many Western countries that I'm aware of.

00:05:44.448 --> 00:05:48.010
But it has not affected everybody.

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:50.680
Some people have managed to remain aware.

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:54.790
They have not been,
one could say, infected

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:59.180
by what one could perhaps
call a mental virus

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:04.180
or mental viruses that
reduce people's ability

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:08.160
to actually see reality.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:11.159
Reality then gets
distorted through the veil

00:06:11.159 --> 00:06:15.393
of these mental viruses that
have taken over people's minds.

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:21.430
This is a more serious pandemic

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:26.610
than anything that happens
on the physical level

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:31.610
as far as pandemics are
concerned, the actual viruses.

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:35.118
Actually, you might, I
don't know if you've read,

00:06:35.118 --> 00:06:40.118
Carl Jung said that the greatest
danger that humanity faces

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:46.148
is not from any external
force like natural disasters

00:06:46.148 --> 00:06:51.060
or diseases or pandemics.

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:54.150
He said the greatest
danger that humanity faces

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:58.023
is a collective psychosis.

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:03.780
So to some extent, I see it
happening, not quite as extreme

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:08.780
yet as in places like
Maoist China or Cambodia

00:07:08.825 --> 00:07:11.475
where 1/3 of the population
got murdered in Cambodia.

00:07:16.714 --> 00:07:21.330
Absurd, totally absurd ideas
taking over people's minds.

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:26.330
For example, in Cambodia, we
were there a few years ago,

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:31.730
at the time of Pol Pot,
the Cambodian mad dictator,

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:39.730
anybody who could read
and write or anybody,

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:42.550
if you wear glasses, you
were an enemy of the people

00:07:42.550 --> 00:07:45.020
because you were regarded as the oppressor

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:47.410
and likely to be killed.

00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:49.343
You had to show your hands.

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:52.390
You're not doing manual work,

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:56.320
you're one of the enemies of the people.

00:07:56.320 --> 00:07:57.872
They sent them away.

00:07:57.872 --> 00:08:01.830
1/3 or more of the
population got exterminated

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:06.783
through insanity taking
over people's minds.

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:12.590
You no longer can see reality as it is.

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:16.750
The famous example from "1984," Orwell,

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:21.063
you have to believe that
two plus two equals five.

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:24.990
- Right.
- And if you don't believe it,

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:27.323
then you are the enemy.

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:31.310
- Which is sort of what
we're being told these days

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:34.710
from some pretty powerful people

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:37.760
and some pretty powerful people
that are pushing bad ideas.

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:39.640
But I suspect that you think

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:42.700
if more people lived in the moment,

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:45.710
if more people harness
the power of now that

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:49.670
that would be the best
inoculation from this mind virus.

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:53.563
- Yes, inoculation to have,

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:59.630
and inoculation is one word one could use.

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:02.420
The key is immunity.

00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:04.710
I think I would use immunity.

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:09.480
The key is what we could call awareness,

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:11.593
or as I'm just calling it, presence.

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:16.883
Awareness or presence
is nothing complicated.

00:09:18.855 --> 00:09:22.997
It's the ability to become
aware of your thoughts

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:27.650
so you can take a step back and to observe

00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:29.780
what thoughts are going through your head.

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:32.547
For example, when this ability arises,

00:09:32.547 --> 00:09:36.300
I call that the beginning
of a spiritual awakening.

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:40.550
Spiritual is no longer
being completely trapped

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:44.493
and identified with the
movement of thinking.

00:09:45.342 --> 00:09:48.100
This is particularly important now.

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:53.100
The danger of infection, viral
infection on a mental level

00:09:56.460 --> 00:10:01.460
has always been there, but
it's now becoming magnified

00:10:01.550 --> 00:10:04.880
by the technology that we now have.

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:07.960
A toxic idea, a toxic thought

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:12.090
can spread like wildfire
through the internet

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:17.090
within a few days and can take possession

00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:22.230
or become lodged in
countless people's minds.

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:24.900
And once a thought has become lodged,

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:28.400
then it will attract associated thoughts

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:33.400
that resonate with it and
then suddenly you see reality

00:10:34.454 --> 00:10:38.670
through the veil of that
irrational thinking,

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:41.260
but you don't know that this is happening

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:45.430
because you do not have
the immunity of awareness.

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:49.500
Awareness is the ability to
know what your mind is doing.

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:51.646
It's also, for example, the ability,

00:10:51.646 --> 00:10:56.646
I think it was Aristotle
who talked about the ability

00:10:56.870 --> 00:10:59.950
of having two conflicting
thoughts in your mind

00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:03.479
without necessarily
identifying with either.

00:11:03.479 --> 00:11:06.800
That implies there is an awareness there.

00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:10.550
Without awareness, one thought
will draw you in completely.

00:11:10.550 --> 00:11:12.720
You will identify with it completely,

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:16.340
and then everything
else is then disregarded

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:19.740
or regarded as threatening.

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:24.740
The egoic self, it identifies
with one particular position.

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:26.990
And this is just one example.

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:29.277
There are many examples one could give.

00:11:29.277 --> 00:11:32.740
It identifies with one position,
and then everything else

00:11:32.740 --> 00:11:36.533
is regarded as whatever the term is.

00:11:37.544 --> 00:11:40.110
What are the favorite terms these days?

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:44.480
Disinformation or whatever,
anyone who disagrees

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:48.637
with my mental position,
that's disinformation.

00:11:48.637 --> 00:11:51.620
We know many examples of that.

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:56.620
- So what's the best way to
immunize yourself against that?

00:11:56.840 --> 00:11:58.270
I mean, I think about that all the time.

00:11:58.270 --> 00:12:01.530
I try to bring information to people

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:03.750
in as honest and decent way as possible.

00:12:03.750 --> 00:12:05.240
And sometimes I think I'm pretty decent,

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:06.980
probably sometimes not so decent,

00:12:06.980 --> 00:12:09.960
but I have no doubt that
I have that veil as well.

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:13.660
And I have probable blind
spots due to my history

00:12:13.660 --> 00:12:15.170
or whatever it might be.

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:18.428
How do you actually climb out of something

00:12:18.428 --> 00:12:21.010
if you're unaware of it at some level?

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:23.513
- Yes, to become aware of one's thinking,

00:12:24.450 --> 00:12:27.180
there's no easy answer to that.

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:29.300
To many people it happens naturally.

00:12:29.300 --> 00:12:32.874
For example, it tends to
happen sometimes to people

00:12:32.874 --> 00:12:37.874
on a personal level whose
thinking becomes so negative

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:42.600
about the, in other words, the
stories they tell themselves.

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:45.981
Let's talk about
narratives that people have

00:12:45.981 --> 00:12:48.100
in their heads, in their minds.

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:49.612
My life is so dreadful

00:12:49.612 --> 00:12:54.612
or I've been treated so
unfairly by society and life

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:58.590
and I've had, everything
bad always happens to me.

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:00.908
I know these things
because when I was young,

00:13:00.908 --> 00:13:03.530
I had similar thoughts in my mind,

00:13:03.530 --> 00:13:06.650
very negative, negative narratives.

00:13:06.650 --> 00:13:10.280
And the more negative narratives
you have, for some people,

00:13:10.280 --> 00:13:13.460
it's the negative narratives
about the world out there,

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:15.530
which is, everything is evil

00:13:15.530 --> 00:13:20.530
and they're out to sabotage me and so on.

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:23.640
Or the negative narrative
may be about myself,

00:13:23.640 --> 00:13:25.410
there's something wrong with me.

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:28.460
Whatever it may be, it
leads to an enormous amount

00:13:28.460 --> 00:13:30.670
of suffering, emotional suffering

00:13:30.670 --> 00:13:32.962
because the emotion is
usually a reflection

00:13:32.962 --> 00:13:36.474
of what you're telling
yourself in your mind

00:13:36.474 --> 00:13:40.485
creates a reflection
on the emotional level.

00:13:40.485 --> 00:13:42.780
So if your narrative is very negative,

00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:47.780
you then experience very negative
emotions, anger, sadness,

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:52.607
resentment, or if your
narrative is very much directed

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:57.910
towards the future, the fearful future,

00:13:57.910 --> 00:14:00.040
then there's a lot of anxiety and fear

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:02.330
because the future is so uncertain.

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:06.790
And so people who go into a
lot of suffering, at some point

00:14:06.790 --> 00:14:11.790
they sometimes realize that
the suffering they experience

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:14.540
is actually produced by their own minds.

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:17.353
For example, somebody might
suddenly wake up and say,

00:14:17.353 --> 00:14:21.820
for the past few hours I've been engaged

00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:25.092
in negative thinking about
myself and the world.

00:14:25.092 --> 00:14:26.980
Wow, isn't that amazing?

00:14:26.980 --> 00:14:30.660
That I have these thoughts
that come back again.

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:33.910
They recur again and again,
thoughts about myself,

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:35.951
things I tell myself about myself.

00:14:35.951 --> 00:14:39.480
And so these thoughts are
creating so much suffering.

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:40.810
You can stand back and see it.

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:42.800
Well, I'm so negative.

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:45.180
Why am I always criticizing people?

00:14:45.180 --> 00:14:47.654
Why am I always complaining
about everything?

00:14:47.654 --> 00:14:51.300
This is the beginning of becoming
aware of what's happening.

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:54.470
Complaining is a big pattern
in many people's minds.

00:14:54.470 --> 00:14:56.124
They love complaining.

00:14:56.124 --> 00:14:58.430
Complaining about what's out there,

00:14:58.430 --> 00:15:01.340
complaining about my life
and pointing about them,

00:15:01.340 --> 00:15:04.720
complaining, and I'm not
talking about complaining

00:15:06.357 --> 00:15:09.810
where you have the ability
to change a situation.

00:15:09.810 --> 00:15:12.670
Then sometimes it's good to speak out

00:15:12.670 --> 00:15:15.360
when there's possibility of change.

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:18.220
But many cases, people just complain

00:15:18.220 --> 00:15:20.440
because it makes the ego feel bigger

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:22.703
because the more I complain about others,

00:15:22.703 --> 00:15:25.710
the bigger my ego feels

00:15:25.710 --> 00:15:28.159
because I'm right and they are all wrong

00:15:28.159 --> 00:15:30.743
and the ego loves to be right.

00:15:31.904 --> 00:15:34.672
- You're perfectly spelling out

00:15:34.672 --> 00:15:38.270
exactly why I get off social
media because we all suffer.

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:39.380
We all suffer from that.

00:15:39.380 --> 00:15:40.830
If I get a lot of retweets,

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:43.250
it has a certain dopamine effect to me,

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:45.180
or I sometimes I open it up

00:15:45.180 --> 00:15:46.800
and I'll look for negative comments

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:49.660
even though I don't consider
myself a negative person.

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:52.120
- Yes, now, but a very important thing.

00:15:52.120 --> 00:15:55.861
When you have interviews
or dialogues with people,

00:15:55.861 --> 00:16:00.861
there's usually, there's
a background field

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:06.460
of a peaceful coming together.

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:10.410
There's a background field of,
there's a certain connective.

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:14.840
Even if your opinion and the
person you're interviewing,

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:17.470
maybe have very different viewpoints,

00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:20.260
very different thoughts, nevertheless,

00:16:20.260 --> 00:16:23.623
you are not so identified
with a viewpoint,

00:16:23.623 --> 00:16:28.623
the mental position, that
anybody who questions

00:16:30.580 --> 00:16:34.110
your viewpoint is unconsciously
regarded as an enemy

00:16:34.110 --> 00:16:38.240
that needs to be defeated so
that you have an awareness,

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:40.815
perhaps you don't call it awareness.

00:16:40.815 --> 00:16:44.443
When you conduct interviews,

00:16:44.443 --> 00:16:49.443
there's still a background field of peace.

00:16:50.010 --> 00:16:52.780
There is not antagonism.

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:57.453
I observed the same, I was
very unhappy to observe,

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:03.140
Russell Brand recently
interviewed Shapiro.

00:17:06.119 --> 00:17:07.180
What's his-
- Oh, Ben Shapiro.

00:17:07.180 --> 00:17:08.981
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- What's his name?

00:17:08.981 --> 00:17:10.170
- Ben Shapiro.
- Ben Shapiro.

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:11.660
- And there was a lot of disagreement,

00:17:11.660 --> 00:17:13.130
but there was a mutual respect.

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:14.680
- They come from completely
different positions.

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:16.150
Russell Brand is on the left,

00:17:16.150 --> 00:17:18.591
obviously Ben Shapiro is on the right.

00:17:18.591 --> 00:17:20.930
And then they reversed it later.

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:23.453
Ben Shapiro had him on his show

00:17:23.453 --> 00:17:26.770
and it was really very pleasant to watch.

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:31.770
They were both able to express
clearly their viewpoints

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:34.270
and their mental positions

00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:36.780
without attacking each other at all.

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:40.890
So there was an undercurrent of awareness,

00:17:40.890 --> 00:17:45.890
as I would call it, which is
a dimension of consciousness

00:17:46.213 --> 00:17:49.273
that is extremely important for humans

00:17:49.273 --> 00:17:52.880
to realize within themselves

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:56.840
because if you're not aware
of what your mind is doing

00:17:56.840 --> 00:18:00.950
so there's some separation
from the mental position,

00:18:00.950 --> 00:18:05.280
which is the thought and
who you are, who you are,

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:10.054
is the aware presence in the
background that frees you

00:18:10.054 --> 00:18:14.340
from being possessed by thoughts,

00:18:14.340 --> 00:18:17.750
by narrative space, by mental positions.

00:18:17.750 --> 00:18:21.610
And so that takes the ego
out of the interaction

00:18:21.610 --> 00:18:24.090
and then you can have
a fruitful interaction.

00:18:24.090 --> 00:18:26.420
So you don't need to
give up your view points

00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:28.190
or your mental positions,

00:18:28.190 --> 00:18:31.360
but not be totally identified with it

00:18:31.360 --> 00:18:34.463
so that anybody who questions
it becomes your enemy.

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:37.410
- It's so interesting because obviously

00:18:37.410 --> 00:18:39.470
you're not a political beast,

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:42.050
but what you're saying
here is so applicable

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:44.230
to everything that
everyone's fighting about

00:18:44.230 --> 00:18:45.360
sort of politically these days.

00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:46.830
But I want to ask you one other thing

00:18:46.830 --> 00:18:48.370
about the state of the
world before we move

00:18:48.370 --> 00:18:50.750
into a little bit of the
technology part of this

00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:52.770
and the off the grid sense, which is that

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:54.160
I think you know a bit about my story.

00:18:54.160 --> 00:18:56.300
I used to consider myself an atheist

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:59.500
for probably most of my adult
life and I don't anymore

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:01.280
for probably about four or five years.

00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:03.583
I would say I'm more of a believer now

00:19:03.583 --> 00:19:05.710
than I've ever been in my adult life.

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:09.580
And I think that is
connected to my ability

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:13.850
to sort of stay sane within a
very polarized political time

00:19:13.850 --> 00:19:15.920
and as someone that puts
their opinions out there.

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:17.970
And I wonder what you think about that,

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:21.870
just sort of what the state
of belief is at the moment

00:19:21.870 --> 00:19:25.070
when we factor in this last
year and a half and lockdowns

00:19:25.070 --> 00:19:27.100
and fearfulness of a disease,

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:30.913
and if I walk outside, this
might happen and, and so on.

00:19:32.070 --> 00:19:37.070
- Yes, it's the belief really should lead

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:43.690
to a little bit of a deeper realization.

00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:46.679
Belief alone is fine.

00:19:46.679 --> 00:19:51.679
To believe that your life
has a purpose is good.

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:55.330
That there is a greater purpose to life

00:19:55.330 --> 00:19:57.070
than just your personal life.

00:19:57.070 --> 00:20:01.800
And somehow your personal
life needs to be in alignment

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:06.290
with a greater purpose
that pervades the universe.

00:20:06.290 --> 00:20:11.290
There is an intelligence
that is transcendent

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:16.850
to sense perceived reality,
that is beyond that.

00:20:17.031 --> 00:20:22.031
An intelligence that
manifests itself in this world

00:20:24.050 --> 00:20:26.640
but is also beyond this world.

00:20:26.640 --> 00:20:29.623
Now, whether we call that vast,

00:20:31.010 --> 00:20:35.600
inconceivable intelligence
God or the divine

00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:40.312
or no name at all doesn't really matter.

00:20:40.312 --> 00:20:44.633
So it's good to believe that it's there.

00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:48.060
And then the next step is
to have a little bit of

00:20:51.003 --> 00:20:56.003
an experience to experience
that which lies beyond the world

00:20:56.720 --> 00:21:01.720
of form, which is physical
forms and even mental forms.

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:05.930
And that which lies
beyond the world of form

00:21:05.930 --> 00:21:09.320
is this transcendent dimension

00:21:09.320 --> 00:21:14.073
that humans can sense within themselves.

00:21:14.073 --> 00:21:17.246
It sounds perhaps a
little abstract right now,

00:21:17.246 --> 00:21:22.246
but you can sense it, for
example, in between two thoughts

00:21:24.010 --> 00:21:26.393
when one thought comes to an end

00:21:26.393 --> 00:21:29.630
and there's a moment of clear awareness.

00:21:29.630 --> 00:21:30.927
You're just, you're looking around.

00:21:30.927 --> 00:21:33.680
Sometimes this happens
when you're out in nature.

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:36.670
You're able to stop thinking for a moment,

00:21:36.670 --> 00:21:38.870
but you don't lose consciousness.

00:21:38.870 --> 00:21:40.470
There's still an awareness there.

00:21:40.470 --> 00:21:42.718
And you perceive everything

00:21:42.718 --> 00:21:45.710
against this background of awareness.

00:21:45.710 --> 00:21:47.645
That is the light of consciousness.

00:21:47.645 --> 00:21:51.345
This is why, again, it does
connect us with religion.

00:21:51.345 --> 00:21:55.517
Jesus said to his disciples,

00:21:55.517 --> 00:21:57.486
"You are the light of the world."

00:21:57.486 --> 00:22:01.070
He's talking to everybody
when he said that.

00:22:01.070 --> 00:22:04.100
Now, this doesn't mean you are
a very special human being,

00:22:04.100 --> 00:22:05.780
you're more special than others

00:22:05.780 --> 00:22:08.040
because the people he talked to

00:22:08.040 --> 00:22:10.597
were not special on a worldly level.

00:22:10.597 --> 00:22:12.250
They were not VIPs.

00:22:12.250 --> 00:22:15.587
They were simpler people, but he said,

00:22:15.587 --> 00:22:17.290
"You are the light of the world."

00:22:17.290 --> 00:22:19.310
In another gospel, he
said it about himself.

00:22:19.310 --> 00:22:20.860
He said, "I am the light of the world."

00:22:20.860 --> 00:22:22.800
So both statements he said.

00:22:22.800 --> 00:22:24.480
Now what does that mean?

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:27.623
If you are the light of the world,

00:22:28.920 --> 00:22:32.150
the light in you is the consciousness,

00:22:32.150 --> 00:22:36.980
the consciousness with which
the world is perceived,

00:22:36.980 --> 00:22:39.093
the consciousness without which

00:22:39.093 --> 00:22:41.420
no sense perception would be possible.

00:22:41.420 --> 00:22:42.740
The consciousness without which

00:22:42.740 --> 00:22:44.898
no thought would be possible.

00:22:44.898 --> 00:22:49.050
So you are this light of consciousness.

00:22:49.050 --> 00:22:51.700
And to sense yourself as the consciousness

00:22:51.700 --> 00:22:56.700
that is far more vast than the personality

00:22:57.000 --> 00:23:01.007
which consists of thought,
movement, to sense yourself

00:23:01.007 --> 00:23:05.470
for a moment sense that inner
stillness but not go to sleep.

00:23:05.470 --> 00:23:08.800
No, very alert, sense
that inner stillness.

00:23:08.800 --> 00:23:11.600
Then you can sense the dimension,

00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:15.170
the inner dimension that is
deeper than the personality.

00:23:15.170 --> 00:23:18.800
And that is the light of
the world that emanates.

00:23:18.800 --> 00:23:22.090
We're going a bit deep
now, but let's do it.

00:23:22.090 --> 00:23:23.470
- Yeah, let's do it.

00:23:23.470 --> 00:23:25.187
- That is the light of the world.

00:23:25.187 --> 00:23:28.060
The light of consciousness that emanates

00:23:28.060 --> 00:23:32.110
from the transcendent source of all lives.

00:23:32.110 --> 00:23:36.950
So to me, God is the
transcendent source of all lives.

00:23:36.950 --> 00:23:40.210
God does not have a
location in space or time.

00:23:40.210 --> 00:23:43.600
God transcends space and time, but God,

00:23:43.600 --> 00:23:46.770
it's a bit like the Sun in
the sense perceived world.

00:23:46.770 --> 00:23:49.500
The Sun emanates life.

00:23:49.500 --> 00:23:54.480
It emanates light which is
life continuously, it emanates.

00:23:54.480 --> 00:23:59.480
Now, let's imagine that
you are a ray of sunlight.

00:24:00.021 --> 00:24:05.021
And suddenly you realize
that who or what you are

00:24:08.550 --> 00:24:09.840
emanates from the Sun.

00:24:09.840 --> 00:24:11.130
Before you didn't know it

00:24:11.130 --> 00:24:14.220
because you thought you
were a disconnected ray,

00:24:14.220 --> 00:24:17.840
just a little spark disconnected.

00:24:17.840 --> 00:24:20.130
And then you become still for a moment

00:24:20.130 --> 00:24:22.060
and you sense the connectedness

00:24:22.060 --> 00:24:24.110
to something much deeper than the person.

00:24:25.086 --> 00:24:27.220
So just a moment of stillness.

00:24:27.220 --> 00:24:30.050
In one of the Psalms in
the Old Testament, it says,

00:24:30.050 --> 00:24:34.510
be still and know that I am God.

00:24:34.510 --> 00:24:37.020
You can only know God in the stillness.

00:24:37.020 --> 00:24:40.510
When you become still then suddenly,

00:24:40.510 --> 00:24:43.940
to go back to the analogy,
the ray of sunlight

00:24:43.940 --> 00:24:48.811
realizes its connectedness
and oneness with the Sun

00:24:48.811 --> 00:24:53.320
And some of the mystics who
discovered that in themselves

00:24:53.320 --> 00:24:56.270
suddenly said, I am God.

00:24:56.270 --> 00:24:58.000
That's not advisable to do.

00:24:58.000 --> 00:25:01.270
And then we usually,
people didn't like that.

00:25:01.270 --> 00:25:03.677
So because the ray of sunlight,

00:25:03.677 --> 00:25:06.530
yes, it's eternally connected.

00:25:06.530 --> 00:25:10.600
It's an emanation of the
Sun, but it's not the Sun.

00:25:10.600 --> 00:25:14.340
You are an emanation or your
consciousness is an emanation

00:25:14.340 --> 00:25:19.290
of the Godhead or God,
but you are not God,

00:25:19.290 --> 00:25:20.770
but you're connected to,

00:25:20.770 --> 00:25:22.890
you are one with God and you're not,

00:25:22.890 --> 00:25:26.727
seemingly paradoxical or
contradictory statements.

00:25:26.727 --> 00:25:31.518
So just the belief is good.

00:25:31.518 --> 00:25:34.460
And then the belief can lead to something

00:25:34.460 --> 00:25:36.430
a little deeper than just the beliefs.

00:25:36.430 --> 00:25:40.790
And then you can rest in
that sense of connectedness

00:25:40.790 --> 00:25:43.980
to something that
transcends the personality.

00:25:43.980 --> 00:25:45.575
You rest in that.

00:25:45.575 --> 00:25:47.830
And that is what is called,

00:25:47.830 --> 00:25:52.030
to me, that is the true meaning of faith.

00:25:52.030 --> 00:25:55.743
Faith to me is not just
an ideological belief

00:25:55.743 --> 00:25:58.223
that this is the case or the belief

00:25:58.223 --> 00:26:02.386
that a certain story from
the past actually happened.

00:26:02.386 --> 00:26:04.640
Faith is trust.

00:26:04.640 --> 00:26:06.980
And the trust comes with the realization

00:26:06.980 --> 00:26:09.730
that there's more to you
than just the personality,

00:26:09.730 --> 00:26:14.730
the person, and to be rooted
in this trust is inner peace.

00:26:15.120 --> 00:26:17.320
And then you can breathe more clearly.

00:26:17.320 --> 00:26:19.960
There are people who are
extremely knowledgeable

00:26:19.960 --> 00:26:22.470
about spirituality and everything else,

00:26:22.470 --> 00:26:26.782
but they have never gone
that little step further

00:26:26.782 --> 00:26:30.870
from recognizing the truth
on an intellectual level,

00:26:30.870 --> 00:26:34.020
which is good, to going
a little bit further

00:26:34.020 --> 00:26:39.020
and realize the truth
experientially in their own lives.

00:26:40.700 --> 00:26:44.159
And that frees them from fear and anxiety.

00:26:44.159 --> 00:26:47.780
It's a wonderful
liberation to realize that,

00:26:47.780 --> 00:26:51.530
maybe not continuously,
but you have more and more,

00:26:51.530 --> 00:26:56.050
you realize there is more
to you than meets the eye,

00:26:56.050 --> 00:26:59.360
so to speak, that you are
not the physical body,

00:26:59.360 --> 00:27:01.550
you're not your mind even.

00:27:01.550 --> 00:27:03.480
There's an invisible presence

00:27:03.480 --> 00:27:05.400
that is the essence of who you are.

00:27:05.400 --> 00:27:08.990
And it's vital for humans to realize that.

00:27:08.990 --> 00:27:10.810
I believe that's the next step

00:27:10.810 --> 00:27:14.772
now that old-fashioned
religions in many countries

00:27:14.772 --> 00:27:19.710
are beginning to disappear,
the old religion,

00:27:19.710 --> 00:27:24.710
but in a way I can see why many humans

00:27:24.930 --> 00:27:27.501
cannot believe these stories anymore,

00:27:27.501 --> 00:27:30.100
but we have to be very careful that the,

00:27:30.100 --> 00:27:32.220
what is the expression?

00:27:32.220 --> 00:27:34.668
Throw out the baby with the bath water.

00:27:34.668 --> 00:27:35.501
- Right.

00:27:35.501 --> 00:27:38.070
- Because there's something
extremely valuable there still.

00:27:38.070 --> 00:27:40.630
This is why I often refer back to

00:27:40.630 --> 00:27:44.060
that it just needs to
be more than ideology.

00:27:44.060 --> 00:27:48.960
We need to take one step
further into that realization.

00:27:48.960 --> 00:27:52.120
So this is a, we could talk
about this for a long time,

00:27:52.120 --> 00:27:55.190
but I don't know whether
this will help anybody,

00:27:55.190 --> 00:27:56.315
but I hope so.

00:27:56.315 --> 00:27:58.730
- Well, first off, of course,
it's gonna help people,

00:27:58.730 --> 00:28:00.460
but really you're describing

00:28:00.460 --> 00:28:03.710
my own personal journey almost to a tee.

00:28:03.710 --> 00:28:05.000
And you're actually also describing

00:28:05.000 --> 00:28:07.790
why this will be my fifth
year doing this off the grid

00:28:07.790 --> 00:28:10.930
August situation because
it was on the first one

00:28:10.930 --> 00:28:14.050
where I was sitting on a beach
and David kept saying to me

00:28:14.050 --> 00:28:15.980
for days, "Why aren't you reading a book?

00:28:15.980 --> 00:28:18.130
You're just sitting and
staring at the ocean."

00:28:18.130 --> 00:28:20.750
And I said, "That's actually
what I need right now."

00:28:20.750 --> 00:28:23.230
And it was truly in that
moment when the thought

00:28:23.230 --> 00:28:25.901
popped into my mind
that I'm not an atheist.

00:28:25.901 --> 00:28:28.450
And I would say in the
five years since then

00:28:28.450 --> 00:28:31.186
have been the most sort
of rewarding and enriching

00:28:31.186 --> 00:28:34.585
and full years that
I've had on this planet.

00:28:34.585 --> 00:28:38.540
So I wonder, to connect
that to what I'm doing

00:28:38.540 --> 00:28:42.508
with this month, I
suppose someone like you

00:28:42.508 --> 00:28:45.320
kinda digs something like this,

00:28:45.320 --> 00:28:47.910
the idea that someone could
put down their devices.

00:28:47.910 --> 00:28:50.230
And I wonder, what do
you think just in general

00:28:50.230 --> 00:28:53.670
about a world that is
so obsessively connected

00:28:53.670 --> 00:28:56.470
to other people's thoughts all day long.

00:28:56.470 --> 00:28:57.490
- Yes, that's good.

00:28:57.490 --> 00:29:02.490
So although this excessive
identification with thinking

00:29:04.950 --> 00:29:07.720
and overthinking, excessive thinking

00:29:07.720 --> 00:29:09.330
has been there for a long time,

00:29:09.330 --> 00:29:12.459
long before we came up with these devices,

00:29:12.459 --> 00:29:17.459
but these devices amplify
the human tendency to engage

00:29:21.130 --> 00:29:25.600
or indulge in excessive thinking
and problem-making thinking

00:29:25.600 --> 00:29:29.603
rather than constructive
thinking, focused thinking.

00:29:30.950 --> 00:29:35.950
So what you are doing
is very, very helpful

00:29:37.600 --> 00:29:41.007
because you are basically
having a period of,

00:29:44.880 --> 00:29:47.520
we could call it decluttering your mind.

00:29:47.520 --> 00:29:49.480
You declutter your mind.

00:29:49.480 --> 00:29:54.155
And this is necessary because
our mind, most people's minds

00:29:54.155 --> 00:29:58.143
have never been as
cluttered as they are now.

00:30:00.189 --> 00:30:05.050
Cluttered means there's a
continuous input of stuff

00:30:05.050 --> 00:30:07.757
that comes in through the devices.

00:30:07.757 --> 00:30:12.757
The messages come in,
Facebook posts, tweets,

00:30:15.580 --> 00:30:18.960
and continuously the devices
demand your attention

00:30:18.960 --> 00:30:21.020
and say, this is important.

00:30:21.020 --> 00:30:23.410
And a lot of it is not important.

00:30:23.410 --> 00:30:28.410
But as we all know, there's
an addictive quality to it.

00:30:28.930 --> 00:30:31.650
It draws your attention to it.

00:30:31.650 --> 00:30:34.175
And then every time it
draws your attention,

00:30:34.175 --> 00:30:36.520
you add to the clutter of your mind.

00:30:36.520 --> 00:30:39.119
A lot of not is not constructive.

00:30:39.119 --> 00:30:41.910
A lot of it is just random.

00:30:41.910 --> 00:30:45.722
People often see people,
they get out their phones

00:30:45.722 --> 00:30:48.460
and they do this random scrolling.

00:30:48.460 --> 00:30:51.230
I can see it's random,
there's nothing specific,

00:30:51.230 --> 00:30:52.500
but they think they have to do it

00:30:52.500 --> 00:30:54.870
because everybody else
is doing it around them.

00:30:54.870 --> 00:30:58.390
Wherever you are these days,
people are engaging with this,

00:30:58.390 --> 00:31:02.470
and they're continuously
taking in thoughts from others.

00:31:02.470 --> 00:31:07.470
And as we said before, some
of these thoughts may be toxic

00:31:07.550 --> 00:31:11.593
and they may easily become
lodged in your mind.

00:31:13.220 --> 00:31:16.053
So to declutter is extremely important.

00:31:17.160 --> 00:31:21.730
And you can see if you're
even just not using a device

00:31:21.730 --> 00:31:25.823
for a day, for many people
it's very, very hard.

00:31:27.260 --> 00:31:29.980
And some think they can
do it, but they can't

00:31:29.980 --> 00:31:31.993
so they are truly addicted.

00:31:34.170 --> 00:31:38.097
Now, when you declutter your mind,

00:31:38.097 --> 00:31:41.590
first of all, you put down
your phone, you don't use it.

00:31:41.590 --> 00:31:44.097
Not everybody can do it
for a whole month like you.

00:31:44.097 --> 00:31:45.350
- Of course, of course.

00:31:45.350 --> 00:31:47.480
- But I recommend to everybody

00:31:47.480 --> 00:31:52.170
to have certain periods of
time when they do not engage.

00:31:52.170 --> 00:31:55.920
So for example, in your
bedroom might be a good place

00:31:55.920 --> 00:31:58.913
to try out for not
engaging with any device.

00:32:00.240 --> 00:32:04.550
Certain periods of time,
when you go out into nature,

00:32:04.550 --> 00:32:07.230
be there rather than carry that thing

00:32:07.230 --> 00:32:09.607
and every time it makes a
noise, you still look up

00:32:09.607 --> 00:32:13.710
and you're still, even while
you're surrounded by beauty

00:32:13.710 --> 00:32:17.200
and aliveliness, you're
still engaging with this

00:32:17.200 --> 00:32:21.230
or everything that you are looking at

00:32:21.230 --> 00:32:24.730
is an opportunity for an Instagram post.

00:32:24.730 --> 00:32:28.000
And you're just looking,
look, I'm here now.

00:32:28.000 --> 00:32:31.617
Me here, me there and
then you send it out.

00:32:32.523 --> 00:32:37.523
So you never again become
completely trapped in the mind

00:32:40.995 --> 00:32:45.995
more than even, with these
devices I'm very concerned

00:32:46.600 --> 00:32:50.105
about youngsters these
days who grow up with them.

00:32:50.105 --> 00:32:51.950
Perhaps this is the first generation.

00:32:51.950 --> 00:32:53.200
I don't know, the first iPhone

00:32:53.200 --> 00:32:56.580
was maybe 12, 13 years
ago, something like that.

00:32:56.580 --> 00:33:01.420
And these many youngsters,
for many youngsters

00:33:01.420 --> 00:33:06.420
the virtual reality is more
important to them than all this,

00:33:07.900 --> 00:33:11.638
and this is a very dangerous development.

00:33:11.638 --> 00:33:16.638
They lose the ability to
relate to other humans.

00:33:16.750 --> 00:33:21.100
They spend several hours
per day on devices,

00:33:21.100 --> 00:33:26.100
whereas before they would go
out, running around outside,

00:33:26.260 --> 00:33:31.260
playing their games, creative,
coming up with new games,

00:33:31.260 --> 00:33:36.260
creative activities, relating
to nature, climbing up trees.

00:33:37.340 --> 00:33:38.870
Yes, it's a little bit of risky.

00:33:38.870 --> 00:33:40.292
You might fall down, but again,

00:33:40.292 --> 00:33:45.180
our society is obsessed
with safety and security.

00:33:45.180 --> 00:33:49.120
But anyway, let's not go
there right now. (laughs)

00:33:49.120 --> 00:33:51.863
So I'm very concerned.

00:33:56.960 --> 00:33:59.500
It's not inconceivable that it could have

00:33:59.500 --> 00:34:03.220
such a detrimental effect on consciousness

00:34:03.220 --> 00:34:06.210
that within two generations,

00:34:06.210 --> 00:34:09.560
it could lead to the
breakdown of civilization

00:34:09.560 --> 00:34:13.570
because humans would no longer
be able to creatively think,

00:34:13.570 --> 00:34:16.230
focus on a specific
problem for long enough

00:34:16.230 --> 00:34:21.230
to find a solution, connect
with a deeper intelligence

00:34:21.380 --> 00:34:25.210
that is necessary to do
anything creative in this world,

00:34:25.210 --> 00:34:28.520
to give attention to something
for a certain period of time

00:34:28.520 --> 00:34:31.870
rather than have short attention periods.

00:34:31.870 --> 00:34:34.550
You can't focus on anything for very long.

00:34:34.550 --> 00:34:38.330
How can you solve a problem
if you cannot look at it,

00:34:38.330 --> 00:34:41.670
face it, and then become
still for a moment,

00:34:41.670 --> 00:34:43.860
activate your deep intelligence

00:34:43.860 --> 00:34:46.216
and then see what the solution might be.

00:34:46.216 --> 00:34:48.553
So if we lose the ability,

00:34:51.107 --> 00:34:53.000
it's the parents' responsibility

00:34:53.000 --> 00:34:56.890
to limit their children's
time with these devices.

00:34:56.890 --> 00:35:01.270
And I would suggest periodically
take them out into nature

00:35:01.270 --> 00:35:05.670
without these things so that
they don't lose their ability

00:35:05.670 --> 00:35:08.020
to connect with nature.

00:35:08.020 --> 00:35:10.850
It's so important to connect with nature

00:35:12.780 --> 00:35:16.620
because you find sanity there.

00:35:16.620 --> 00:35:19.530
That was my saving thing
when I was a child.

00:35:19.530 --> 00:35:20.670
I would get on my bike.

00:35:20.670 --> 00:35:23.180
I was very unhappy in my home environment.

00:35:23.180 --> 00:35:25.053
It was very dysfunctional.

00:35:26.040 --> 00:35:27.360
My parents couldn't help it.

00:35:27.360 --> 00:35:30.070
They were just in the grip of dysfunction

00:35:30.070 --> 00:35:33.310
and their parents had been
in the grip of dysfunction.

00:35:33.310 --> 00:35:35.920
And so I would get on my
bike, go out into nature,

00:35:35.920 --> 00:35:38.220
like a 15-minute bike ride.

00:35:38.220 --> 00:35:40.230
Not magnificent, fantastic nature,

00:35:40.230 --> 00:35:45.230
just normal fields, groves of trees.

00:35:45.540 --> 00:35:49.077
And there I would suddenly
get off my bike and say, "Ah."

00:35:50.360 --> 00:35:52.912
I didn't have any devices to distract me.

00:35:52.912 --> 00:35:54.030
There weren't any.

00:35:54.030 --> 00:35:56.807
I would actually be there and look.

00:35:56.807 --> 00:36:01.150
And I would often say to myself,
this will always be here.

00:36:01.150 --> 00:36:02.681
I didn't know what that meant.

00:36:02.681 --> 00:36:06.260
I could feel that nature
was more important

00:36:06.260 --> 00:36:08.887
than the man-made world,
the human-made world.

00:36:08.887 --> 00:36:11.923
The human-made world for
me was a very unhappy one.

00:36:12.820 --> 00:36:14.650
And the natural world

00:36:14.650 --> 00:36:19.354
was where I found liberation
whenever I went there.

00:36:19.354 --> 00:36:21.770
But if I'd had these phones,

00:36:21.770 --> 00:36:23.627
I would have carried that with me

00:36:23.627 --> 00:36:27.163
and probably no longer be
able to really relate to it.

00:36:28.220 --> 00:36:30.980
- You'll be happy to know
that by the time we air this,

00:36:30.980 --> 00:36:33.625
I will probably be sitting in a tree house

00:36:33.625 --> 00:36:36.650
in a rain forest, doing exactly this.

00:36:36.650 --> 00:36:39.240
I mean, this is exactly
why I wanted to talk to you

00:36:39.240 --> 00:36:40.350
before I went off the grid.

00:36:40.350 --> 00:36:41.183
But you mentioned something

00:36:41.183 --> 00:36:42.490
that I thought was really
interesting which is

00:36:42.490 --> 00:36:46.150
that it's not just that
we're being inundated

00:36:46.150 --> 00:36:47.860
with other people's thoughts,

00:36:47.860 --> 00:36:51.370
but that we're never
giving ourself the space,

00:36:51.370 --> 00:36:53.790
the moments where in the
old days, if you said

00:36:53.790 --> 00:36:55.670
you were gonna meet your
friend at a restaurant, well,

00:36:55.670 --> 00:36:58.290
if you went to the restaurant
first and they weren't there,

00:36:58.290 --> 00:36:59.930
you might have to sit for a few moments.

00:36:59.930 --> 00:37:02.150
You might have to perhaps
talk to somebody else,

00:37:02.150 --> 00:37:05.120
but you might have to just
stand and look around and think

00:37:05.120 --> 00:37:08.080
and see people where now
we don't do that at all.

00:37:08.080 --> 00:37:10.020
What do we all immediately do?

00:37:10.020 --> 00:37:12.990
So it's really about creating
that space in many ways

00:37:12.990 --> 00:37:16.820
is more important than inoculating

00:37:16.820 --> 00:37:18.430
or immunizing the thoughts.

00:37:18.430 --> 00:37:21.360
That's almost the obvious
one, it's the other piece.

00:37:21.360 --> 00:37:23.560
- Exactly, that's very important.

00:37:23.560 --> 00:37:25.930
And that is something that anybody can do

00:37:25.930 --> 00:37:27.393
to create that space.

00:37:29.988 --> 00:37:31.448
It's very true what you say.

00:37:31.448 --> 00:37:36.448
Almost nowhere do you see people,
wherever people congregate

00:37:37.430 --> 00:37:42.430
at airports, cafes, benches, park benches,

00:37:43.420 --> 00:37:45.010
wherever they are, most of them

00:37:45.010 --> 00:37:48.390
are getting engaged with their
devices, it's incredible.

00:37:48.390 --> 00:37:53.390
So to consciously decide
not to engage whenever,

00:37:53.460 --> 00:37:55.880
for example, you're waiting
for something or someone.

00:37:55.880 --> 00:37:57.680
And a lot of the time we are waiting

00:37:57.680 --> 00:37:59.418
for things in this world.

00:37:59.418 --> 00:38:02.508
You're waiting for somebody,
as you said an example,

00:38:02.508 --> 00:38:05.497
for a friend to arrive
and you're sitting there,

00:38:05.497 --> 00:38:07.070
why do you need to engage?

00:38:07.070 --> 00:38:11.490
Why can't you just be,
contemplate the world, look around

00:38:11.490 --> 00:38:16.180
and be, and enjoy being in
the moment in this moment.

00:38:16.180 --> 00:38:18.665
And those are the states

00:38:18.665 --> 00:38:22.370
where creative insights often arise.

00:38:22.370 --> 00:38:25.920
If you don't give yourself
space, it's very unlikely

00:38:25.920 --> 00:38:30.920
that any creative
realizations, ideas, insights,

00:38:31.240 --> 00:38:34.120
realizations will arise in you

00:38:34.120 --> 00:38:36.950
because your mind is too cluttered.

00:38:36.950 --> 00:38:40.390
So if you give yourself
space, it's more likely

00:38:40.390 --> 00:38:44.160
that you will become more
creative as a human being

00:38:44.160 --> 00:38:47.500
because that's where these
things, without space,

00:38:47.500 --> 00:38:52.500
good new ideas, insights,
and realizations don't arise.

00:38:53.090 --> 00:38:55.091
There's no room for them to arise.

00:38:55.091 --> 00:38:57.900
So give yourself, a wonderful example,

00:38:57.900 --> 00:39:00.150
you're waiting for somebody, just be there

00:39:00.150 --> 00:39:03.070
unless there's actually
something to communicate.

00:39:03.070 --> 00:39:07.100
Maybe he's texting you, he
says, I'll be five minutes late.

00:39:07.100 --> 00:39:09.883
Fine, okay, and then you put it away.

00:39:11.130 --> 00:39:14.620
I often recommend anytime you're waiting,

00:39:14.620 --> 00:39:19.620
just be conscious of yourself
in the present moment.

00:39:20.490 --> 00:39:24.590
Elevators even, you press the button,

00:39:24.590 --> 00:39:26.233
elevator, and you're waiting.

00:39:27.100 --> 00:39:30.180
Why do you need to get out
your phone for a thought

00:39:30.180 --> 00:39:33.130
half a minute or one minute, why?

00:39:33.130 --> 00:39:36.403
You don't need, just
be, breathe consciously.

00:39:37.419 --> 00:39:40.788
Have a little bit of
inner space, inner space.

00:39:40.788 --> 00:39:44.180
The loss of inner space
is a terrible loss,

00:39:44.180 --> 00:39:48.549
and that is the opposite of clutter.

00:39:48.549 --> 00:39:53.170
Make sure that you become
aware of this inner space

00:39:53.170 --> 00:39:54.200
where there's no clutter.

00:39:54.200 --> 00:39:57.740
There's just a lovely, aware presence

00:39:57.740 --> 00:40:00.295
when you contemplate the world around you,

00:40:00.295 --> 00:40:03.220
you're aware perhaps
that you're breathing.

00:40:03.220 --> 00:40:05.880
You're aware even perhaps
that your body is alive.

00:40:05.880 --> 00:40:09.700
You can sense that your
body is alive, inner space.

00:40:09.700 --> 00:40:14.240
Without spaciousness, your
life is very unsatisfying.

00:40:14.240 --> 00:40:17.400
The most satisfying thing in
life is inner spaciousness,

00:40:17.400 --> 00:40:21.680
and many humans don't have that anymore.

00:40:21.680 --> 00:40:23.929
- And we all know that it's true.

00:40:23.929 --> 00:40:26.440
If we would take that
moment to think about it,

00:40:26.440 --> 00:40:28.080
what you're describing,
we all know is true.

00:40:28.080 --> 00:40:29.680
You know, in the years
that I've done this,

00:40:29.680 --> 00:40:32.240
when I come back in
September, I always notice

00:40:32.240 --> 00:40:34.090
I have a certain force field

00:40:34.090 --> 00:40:37.030
where I'm able to put
the device down more.

00:40:37.030 --> 00:40:39.280
I'm able to pay less
attention, but then of course,

00:40:39.280 --> 00:40:40.640
you know, the news starts again

00:40:40.640 --> 00:40:43.020
or there's an election
or something happened.

00:40:43.020 --> 00:40:45.130
And then it gets sort
of smaller and smaller.

00:40:45.130 --> 00:40:47.450
But I'm wondering as
you're discussing this,

00:40:47.450 --> 00:40:50.210
how much of this is just
that we have to battle

00:40:50.210 --> 00:40:51.940
what our own nature is in a way,

00:40:51.940 --> 00:40:53.770
that we have to battle what the ego is?

00:40:53.770 --> 00:40:57.060
So for example, if you go
to a concert for a musician

00:40:57.060 --> 00:41:00.660
or a band that you love,
instead of just being there

00:41:00.660 --> 00:41:04.700
and just being there,
we're all taking the video,

00:41:04.700 --> 00:41:06.040
we're all taking the pictures

00:41:06.040 --> 00:41:07.950
'cause we want the likes and all that.

00:41:07.950 --> 00:41:12.120
And that we're actually sort
of denigrating the thing

00:41:12.120 --> 00:41:14.720
that gives us that
transcendent experience.

00:41:14.720 --> 00:41:15.943
- [Eckhart] Yes.

00:41:15.943 --> 00:41:16.860
- So we're battling
something within ourselves.

00:41:16.860 --> 00:41:19.750
- Yes, it's certain conditioned patterns

00:41:19.750 --> 00:41:23.614
that we kind of collectively
inherit where it's,

00:41:23.614 --> 00:41:25.742
we're born into this world.

00:41:25.742 --> 00:41:30.360
And at an early age, we
already become conditioned

00:41:30.360 --> 00:41:33.490
by these collective
patterns that are part,

00:41:33.490 --> 00:41:35.940
some belong to our family and background,

00:41:35.940 --> 00:41:39.710
some belong to the general
culture that we grow up in.

00:41:39.710 --> 00:41:41.308
So we become conditioned,

00:41:41.308 --> 00:41:44.620
and to become aware of
one's own conditioning,

00:41:44.620 --> 00:41:46.826
and again, the key word is aware.

00:41:46.826 --> 00:41:49.820
If you become aware of your conditioning,

00:41:49.820 --> 00:41:52.654
you're no longer totally in
the grip of your conditioning.

00:41:52.654 --> 00:41:57.654
It may still operate, yes,
but you're one foot out

00:41:58.337 --> 00:42:01.477
and one foot in the
conditioning, if you are aware.

00:42:01.477 --> 00:42:04.633
And the example you gave
is also interesting.

00:42:04.633 --> 00:42:08.840
Whenever people see
something, the thing is there,

00:42:08.840 --> 00:42:13.377
they need to videotape, video or take

00:42:14.780 --> 00:42:17.820
for selfies or snapshot.

00:42:17.820 --> 00:42:21.210
So many people have lost the ability

00:42:21.210 --> 00:42:25.806
to experience something
because everything that arises

00:42:25.806 --> 00:42:30.806
is looked at as a possibility
for a photo or video.

00:42:31.610 --> 00:42:34.900
And everything is experienced
through the screen.

00:42:34.900 --> 00:42:36.950
When people go on
vacation often you can see

00:42:36.950 --> 00:42:41.950
that they walk around maybe
the most magnificent place.

00:42:43.570 --> 00:42:45.440
And instead of experiencing fully,

00:42:45.440 --> 00:42:46.760
they experience it through this.

00:42:46.760 --> 00:42:50.390
And perhaps the idea is, when
I get home and I look at this,

00:42:50.390 --> 00:42:52.973
then I'll be able to
experience it fully, and-

00:42:52.973 --> 00:42:55.380
(Dave laughing)
You can't do that either

00:42:57.050 --> 00:42:59.570
- And it never, it never works that way.

00:42:59.570 --> 00:43:00.640
It never works that way.

00:43:00.640 --> 00:43:02.100
We're trying to hold onto something

00:43:02.100 --> 00:43:03.703
that we're not fully
grasping in the first place.

00:43:03.703 --> 00:43:07.060
- Yes, and of course
obviously it's nice sometimes

00:43:07.060 --> 00:43:11.670
to be able to film something,
it's sometimes nice.

00:43:11.670 --> 00:43:16.670
I, sometimes, one of my favorite
subjects for taking photos

00:43:17.680 --> 00:43:20.450
is the sky, I love the
sky and the different,

00:43:20.450 --> 00:43:24.200
the clouds and the different formations.

00:43:24.200 --> 00:43:28.234
I have hundreds of photos of
the sky that I take on my phone

00:43:28.234 --> 00:43:31.090
but I'm not absorbed by it.

00:43:31.090 --> 00:43:33.550
I look at the sky maybe for five minutes,

00:43:33.550 --> 00:43:35.330
I enjoy the beauty of it.

00:43:35.330 --> 00:43:37.140
And then I get out my phone and I think,

00:43:37.140 --> 00:43:40.941
wow, this is so wonderful and that's fine.

00:43:40.941 --> 00:43:45.941
But I'm not treating it
as a photo opportunity

00:43:46.644 --> 00:43:49.184
or a selfie opportunity.

00:43:49.184 --> 00:43:52.287
Not that there's anything
wrong with occasional selfies,

00:43:52.287 --> 00:43:55.793
but if the whole thing
takes over your life,

00:43:55.793 --> 00:43:58.295
then that is dreadful.

00:43:58.295 --> 00:44:00.770
- Right, I have a feeling
I wouldn't see you

00:44:00.770 --> 00:44:02.968
wandering down the street taking selfies

00:44:02.968 --> 00:44:06.020
with the clouds as the
less important part.

00:44:06.020 --> 00:44:09.310
- I always say that the first, you know,

00:44:09.310 --> 00:44:14.310
the myth of the ancient Greek
myth of Narcissus, the man,

00:44:14.750 --> 00:44:17.970
this is where the term
narcissism comes from which,

00:44:17.970 --> 00:44:20.400
narcissism being an extreme form of ego.

00:44:20.400 --> 00:44:23.460
So Narcissus was a beautiful young man.

00:44:23.460 --> 00:44:25.187
He was very happy.

00:44:25.187 --> 00:44:28.760
And one day he was walking
and he saw a pool of water.

00:44:28.760 --> 00:44:29.890
This is of course a time,

00:44:29.890 --> 00:44:32.290
there were not any mirrors at that time.

00:44:32.290 --> 00:44:35.810
In a pool of water he
saw his own reflection.

00:44:35.810 --> 00:44:37.620
And the story goes,

00:44:37.620 --> 00:44:40.133
says he fell in love
with his own reflection.

00:44:42.130 --> 00:44:43.900
Better way of putting it is,

00:44:43.900 --> 00:44:46.860
he became obsessed with
his own reflection.

00:44:46.860 --> 00:44:50.080
And from then on, he became very unhappy

00:44:50.080 --> 00:44:52.800
and his life didn't go well after that.

00:44:52.800 --> 00:44:55.230
We don't need to go into
what happened to him,

00:44:55.230 --> 00:44:57.030
but it wasn't good.

00:44:57.030 --> 00:45:01.280
Now, this is a symbolic way of expressing

00:45:01.280 --> 00:45:05.290
what happened to human consciousness
when the ego developed.

00:45:05.290 --> 00:45:09.640
The ego is an image of
who you are in your mind.

00:45:09.640 --> 00:45:11.360
It's a self image.

00:45:11.360 --> 00:45:15.223
And when Narcissus saw himself,

00:45:16.680 --> 00:45:18.790
the myth is a symbolic expression

00:45:18.790 --> 00:45:20.790
of what happened to human consciousness.

00:45:22.659 --> 00:45:23.853
As the ego developed,

00:45:26.090 --> 00:45:28.883
then you'd suddenly have
an image of who you are.

00:45:30.020 --> 00:45:33.620
I call it the first selfie
ever was when Narcissus

00:45:33.620 --> 00:45:38.620
saw his own reflection
in the pool of water.

00:45:38.790 --> 00:45:43.790
And this also, the
living through a persona,

00:45:45.730 --> 00:45:48.410
which a persona, it's where
the word person comes from.

00:45:48.410 --> 00:45:51.433
And the Latin word persona
actually means mask.

00:45:52.620 --> 00:45:55.500
Living through a mental
image of who you are

00:45:55.500 --> 00:45:58.510
and projecting this mental
image, that was already there

00:45:58.510 --> 00:46:01.470
before we came up with all these devices.

00:46:01.470 --> 00:46:04.330
But now it's become
amplified because many,

00:46:04.330 --> 00:46:06.650
especially many young people,

00:46:06.650 --> 00:46:09.940
they live through Facebook and Instagram,

00:46:09.940 --> 00:46:12.080
and they create an image for themselves

00:46:12.080 --> 00:46:14.600
that they project out into the world.

00:46:14.600 --> 00:46:19.520
And it totally bears little resemblance

00:46:19.520 --> 00:46:21.318
to who they actually are.

00:46:21.318 --> 00:46:23.500
Now there's the added thing,

00:46:23.500 --> 00:46:27.690
they can use filters and Photoshop.

00:46:27.690 --> 00:46:29.280
Everybody can look beautiful.

00:46:29.280 --> 00:46:30.640
Even I could look beautiful

00:46:30.640 --> 00:46:32.420
with a little bit of that filter.

00:46:32.420 --> 00:46:35.780
And often you wouldn't recognize these

00:46:35.780 --> 00:46:40.405
if you saw them in the
street, totally distorted,

00:46:40.405 --> 00:46:42.480
but they live through it.

00:46:42.480 --> 00:46:46.030
It becomes more important to
them than their own being.

00:46:46.030 --> 00:46:51.030
And ultimately it makes
humans very unhappy to live-

00:46:52.860 --> 00:46:53.720
- Well, I realized.

00:46:53.720 --> 00:46:54.970
I mean, that in many ways

00:46:54.970 --> 00:46:56.790
is why I wanted to start doing this

00:46:56.790 --> 00:46:59.210
because I realized as someone
that talks to the camera

00:46:59.210 --> 00:47:02.060
and people say nice things
to me and, you know,

00:47:02.060 --> 00:47:03.940
I get traction on Twitter
and all of those things,

00:47:03.940 --> 00:47:07.140
I felt that I was not, I
wasn't trying to control it,

00:47:07.140 --> 00:47:09.250
but it was becoming
sort of bigger than me,

00:47:09.250 --> 00:47:10.510
which is why I want to do this.

00:47:10.510 --> 00:47:12.190
So actually I only want
to ask you one more thing

00:47:12.190 --> 00:47:13.920
'cause I want to be
respectful of your time.

00:47:13.920 --> 00:47:15.580
But for most of my audience

00:47:15.580 --> 00:47:17.640
what I sense people are
going through right now

00:47:17.640 --> 00:47:22.640
is they're deeply worried
that the world that they knew

00:47:23.210 --> 00:47:25.660
is disappearing at a very rapid rate.

00:47:25.660 --> 00:47:28.050
You sort of hinted at something
like that at the beginning.

00:47:28.050 --> 00:47:30.800
That the things that they
cared about about freedom

00:47:30.800 --> 00:47:34.060
and the individual, that
these things are going away

00:47:34.060 --> 00:47:36.389
and it's being amplified by social media

00:47:36.389 --> 00:47:39.470
and bad political leaders
and everything else.

00:47:39.470 --> 00:47:43.090
What would you say is a way to battle it

00:47:43.090 --> 00:47:45.530
without becoming consumed by it?

00:47:45.530 --> 00:47:47.340
That's what I try to do
on my show all the time.

00:47:47.340 --> 00:47:49.490
I always try to do it with
a little bit of a smile

00:47:49.490 --> 00:47:51.070
and a little sense of humor

00:47:51.070 --> 00:47:53.100
because I don't want people to be crazy,

00:47:53.100 --> 00:47:55.150
but I'm obviously not perfect at this.

00:47:55.150 --> 00:47:56.490
What would you say to the average person

00:47:56.490 --> 00:47:57.560
that wants to be aware?

00:47:57.560 --> 00:48:00.050
They want to be engaged in
current events and politics

00:48:00.050 --> 00:48:03.170
but also don't want to give
their life to it at the expense

00:48:03.170 --> 00:48:05.540
of everything else that
you've discussed here.

00:48:05.540 --> 00:48:07.630
- Yes, do everything with awareness

00:48:07.630 --> 00:48:11.160
so that instead of being reactive,

00:48:11.160 --> 00:48:13.680
let's say you see
somebody posting something

00:48:13.680 --> 00:48:15.723
and you feel you want to reply.

00:48:17.260 --> 00:48:20.780
Don't be reactive and attack somebody

00:48:20.780 --> 00:48:23.990
that you have never even met.

00:48:23.990 --> 00:48:28.990
And don't equate somebody's
perhaps erroneous opinion

00:48:31.002 --> 00:48:33.780
with who they actually are.

00:48:33.780 --> 00:48:37.823
I think it may be, if you
feel called upon to do that,

00:48:37.823 --> 00:48:42.050
it may be good to point
out what you regard

00:48:42.050 --> 00:48:45.538
as irrational statements
that are irrational,

00:48:45.538 --> 00:48:49.540
point out viewpoints
that you think are toxic

00:48:51.646 --> 00:48:55.610
without attacking the human
being that has these viewpoints.

00:48:55.610 --> 00:48:58.130
You can attack opinions and viewpoints

00:48:58.130 --> 00:49:03.073
or show them that they are erroneous

00:49:04.703 --> 00:49:07.247
without making the people who have them

00:49:07.247 --> 00:49:11.310
into absolute evil beings.

00:49:11.310 --> 00:49:16.310
To separate what happens
on the level of mind

00:49:16.563 --> 00:49:20.940
from the human being underneath.

00:49:20.940 --> 00:49:22.690
It's easier to do that

00:49:22.690 --> 00:49:24.940
when you're actually meeting a human being

00:49:26.450 --> 00:49:29.023
because you can see there's the,

00:49:30.100 --> 00:49:33.790
I sometimes call it the
human and the being.

00:49:33.790 --> 00:49:35.440
Everybody is a human being.

00:49:35.440 --> 00:49:40.313
The human is the conditioned
mind, the personality,

00:49:40.313 --> 00:49:43.620
the conditioned entity is a human.

00:49:43.620 --> 00:49:47.880
And the being is the
consciousness that's beyond that.

00:49:47.880 --> 00:49:52.170
That's the deeper being,
that's the, a monk would say

00:49:52.170 --> 00:49:55.970
the true human that's a child of God.

00:49:55.970 --> 00:49:57.830
Every human is a child of God,

00:49:57.830 --> 00:50:02.530
but the overlay may be very,
very dense of conditioning.

00:50:02.530 --> 00:50:04.610
That's the human level.

00:50:04.610 --> 00:50:08.470
It's easier not to lose
sight of the being dimension

00:50:08.470 --> 00:50:11.590
in another human when you
see them face to face.

00:50:11.590 --> 00:50:14.261
Then perhaps you can still sense it.

00:50:14.261 --> 00:50:19.261
But when you're only
relating to abstract words,

00:50:19.462 --> 00:50:22.227
often, on the screen,

00:50:22.227 --> 00:50:26.803
then you confuse what's
produced by the human level.

00:50:30.330 --> 00:50:33.643
You lose sight of their being completely.

00:50:39.310 --> 00:50:42.240
There's an observed
statement that you read

00:50:42.240 --> 00:50:46.330
and you feel that you
want to clarify that.

00:50:46.330 --> 00:50:48.260
It's perfectly fine to do that

00:50:48.260 --> 00:50:49.740
if you feel called upon to do it,

00:50:49.740 --> 00:50:51.700
if you think it has a purpose to do that.

00:50:51.700 --> 00:50:54.263
Sometimes it might,
sometimes it might not,

00:50:55.670 --> 00:50:58.719
without making the person
who has that opinion

00:50:58.719 --> 00:51:01.680
into an enemy, although he or she

00:51:01.680 --> 00:51:04.785
will try to make you
into an enemy, of course.

00:51:04.785 --> 00:51:08.100
In other words, don't
contribute to the insanity.

00:51:08.100 --> 00:51:10.335
Bring sanity into this world.

00:51:10.335 --> 00:51:14.570
Do not allow the insanity to pull you in

00:51:14.570 --> 00:51:17.394
because that can easily happen.

00:51:17.394 --> 00:51:22.394
It pulls you in and then
the monster that you,

00:51:23.180 --> 00:51:25.430
in other words, I don't
remember who said it-

00:51:27.165 --> 00:51:27.998
- If you gaze to, yeah.
- When you fight monsters

00:51:27.998 --> 00:51:30.843
be careful that you
don't become a monster.

00:51:32.917 --> 00:51:36.460
Or Nietzsche said, "When
you look into the abyss

00:51:36.460 --> 00:51:41.110
then the abyss also looks into
you" or something like that.

00:51:41.110 --> 00:51:43.083
So that is certainly the case.

00:51:44.310 --> 00:51:48.360
So I think to bear in mind,

00:51:48.360 --> 00:51:53.240
to bring sanity into
this world is your job.

00:51:53.240 --> 00:51:58.240
To bring sanity into,
well, that in many ways

00:51:59.200 --> 00:52:01.460
is going in the opposite direction

00:52:01.460 --> 00:52:03.030
is becoming more and more crazy.

00:52:03.030 --> 00:52:08.030
So it's doubly important
for you to represent,

00:52:08.300 --> 00:52:13.240
to embody the sanity and always be aware

00:52:13.240 --> 00:52:17.421
of the gravitational pull of craziness,

00:52:17.421 --> 00:52:19.780
which is there all around you.

00:52:19.780 --> 00:52:24.780
And the gravitational pull,
it's the reactivity that comes.

00:52:25.660 --> 00:52:27.446
You don't need that.

00:52:27.446 --> 00:52:32.446
Give yourself a moment
when you feel reactive.

00:52:32.640 --> 00:52:36.847
Before you post anything,
give yourself a few minutes

00:52:36.847 --> 00:52:39.930
to calm down, become present,

00:52:39.930 --> 00:52:44.199
and then see what useful
contribution you could make

00:52:44.199 --> 00:52:47.883
to this particular
discussion on what it may be.

00:52:49.070 --> 00:52:50.520
So who said it?

00:52:50.520 --> 00:52:53.107
I don't remember the famous phrase,

00:52:53.107 --> 00:52:57.020
be the change that you
want to see in this world.

00:52:57.020 --> 00:52:58.720
Maybe it was Nelson Mandela.

00:52:58.720 --> 00:53:01.620
I don't remember quite who
said it, but it doesn't matter.

00:53:03.546 --> 00:53:06.110
So if you want more sanity in this world,

00:53:06.110 --> 00:53:10.991
and if you see that there's a
lot of insanity in this world,

00:53:10.991 --> 00:53:15.991
then it's your job not to
become part of the insanity.

00:53:17.160 --> 00:53:22.160
You cannot fight insanity
with more insanity.

00:53:22.350 --> 00:53:26.686
So be aware, be present, be conscious,

00:53:26.686 --> 00:53:31.020
and don't be totally identified
with your mental positions,

00:53:31.020 --> 00:53:33.410
but express them clearly.

00:53:33.410 --> 00:53:36.410
But realize who you are is far deeper

00:53:36.410 --> 00:53:37.950
than your mental positions.

00:53:37.950 --> 00:53:42.420
They are relatively important
but not absolutely important.

00:53:42.420 --> 00:53:45.390
One thing that's absolutely
important is your being.

00:53:45.390 --> 00:53:50.390
There's the human and there's
the being, you are both.

00:53:50.440 --> 00:53:55.440
And you can exist in both
dimensions consciously

00:53:55.949 --> 00:54:00.949
in the being and be
active on the human level

00:54:01.350 --> 00:54:04.040
without losing yourself
on the human level,

00:54:04.040 --> 00:54:06.770
which is the mind, which is the world,

00:54:06.770 --> 00:54:10.310
which is the internet,
that's all the human level.

00:54:10.310 --> 00:54:12.760
So be a real human being

00:54:12.760 --> 00:54:17.103
so that the two dimensions
are active in you.

00:54:18.144 --> 00:54:20.010
- Well, Eckhart, you know, it's funny.

00:54:20.010 --> 00:54:22.750
I asked you to explain it for my audience,

00:54:22.750 --> 00:54:24.760
and I know you were talking
directly to them there,

00:54:24.760 --> 00:54:27.380
but I genuinely felt like you
were talking directly to me.

00:54:27.380 --> 00:54:31.270
And that's exactly why I do
this off the grid for 30 days.

00:54:31.270 --> 00:54:34.320
And I give you my word that
I will be trying to connect

00:54:34.320 --> 00:54:36.110
to my human and my being.

00:54:36.110 --> 00:54:41.110
And what a great way to leave
for me so I thank you so much,

00:54:42.800 --> 00:54:45.560
and I promise you that
I'm gonna incorporate that

00:54:45.560 --> 00:54:47.780
even further when I get back in the fall.

00:54:47.780 --> 00:54:50.920
- Right, and have a wonderful
time on your retreat.

00:54:50.920 --> 00:54:52.520
- Thank you, my friend.
- Thank you.

